{
  "A row of stars for entering or displaying a score, in whole or half steps. Rating is a field, so the label, help text, rules and `x-model` work the same way as on any other field.": "",
  "Every prop accepts a value or a function, and `x-model` provides two-way binding for the score. On hover, the stars preview the score a click would set.": "",
  "Half stars, sizes and tones": "",
  "Custom icons": "",
  "Increases or decreases the score by one step (by half with `step={0.5}`).": "",
  "Sets no stars (the minimum, without `allowClear`), or all stars.": "",
  "Sets that number of stars.": "",
  "Clears the score (with `allowClear`).": "",
  "A `slider` from 0 to `max`, named by its label. The value is announced as “3 of 5” or “Not rated” in the kit language.": "",
  "`aria-readonly`. The stars only display the score.": "",
  "The field. `data-tone`, `data-size`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`.": "Field. `data-tone`, `data-size`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`.",
  "The row of stars, which is the slider and receives focus.": "",
  "One star, its empty shape and its filled part (`--_fill`: the filled share).": "",
  "Units: the row (focus, disabled), a star growing on hover, the empty shape, and the filled part in each tone.": "",
  "A star and the space between stars, per size.": "Boyuta göre yıldız ve yıldızlar arası boşluk.",
  "The default tone.": "",
  "Place: the field below a rating, without a box.": "",
  "The score, rounded to `step`. `null` means no score. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The number of stars.": "",
  "`0.5` allows half stars, using the first half of a star or the arrow keys.": "",
  "Clicking the selected value, or pressing Delete or Backspace, clears the score.": "",
  "On hover, the stars preview the score a click would set.": "",
  "`accent` or `neutral`. For custom gold stars, set the color in `rating.fill.accent.bg`.": "",
  "The shape of an empty and a filled star: a name from the kit's icon set, or an image address (drawn in the star colors).": "",
  "All standard field props, because a rating is a field.": ""
